    "summary": "A cotton (tabby) batik skirt cloth, a &#039;kain panjang&#039;; hand-drawn on both sides, unsewn.  Decorated with a bold all-over pattern of large flower shapes on stems in bands across the width of the cloth, with stems alternately at top and bottom of cloth.  Stems and outlines in indigo black, petals in soga, seed heads and detail in some petals in white.  Isen pattern filling entire background is gringsing with cross in each scale.  Plain white band around whole edge.  [Text written by Dr Fiona Kerlogue, Horniman Museum.]",
